From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] jail: allow the GPU scanout refresh timer syscalls

The GPU worker creates and arms a monotonic timer for deferred scanouts.
The inherited GPU policy omitted timerfd_create and timerfd_settime, so
the sandbox killed every GPU worker before it could render a frame.
Allow only the clock, flags and relative timer operation used by base::Timer.

Co-Authored-By: gpt-6-astra <noreply@openai.com>
---
--- a/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy
+++ b/jail/seccomp/aarch64/gpu_common.policy
@@ -110,3 +110,7 @@
 
 ## Rules for mali shader dump (debug workflow)
 mkdirat: 1
+
+# The GPU scanout refresh timer uses a nonblocking monotonic timerfd (CLOCK_MONOTONIC = 1).
+timerfd_create: arg0 == 1 && arg1 == O_CLOEXEC|O_NONBLOCK
+timerfd_settime: arg1 == 0
--- a/jail/seccomp/x86_64/gpu_common.policy
+++ b/jail/seccomp/x86_64/gpu_common.policy
@@ -122,3 +122,7 @@
 userfaultfd: 1
 # 0xc018aa3f == UFFDIO_API, 0xaa00 == USERFAULTFD_IOC_NEW
 ioctl: arg1 == 0xc018aa3f || arg1 == 0xaa00
+
+# The GPU scanout refresh timer uses a nonblocking monotonic timerfd (CLOCK_MONOTONIC = 1).
+timerfd_create: arg0 == 1 && arg1 == O_CLOEXEC|O_NONBLOCK
+timerfd_settime: arg1 == 0
